# CI/CD Pipeline Overview

## Purpose
The Jenkins pipeline standardises how client services are built and deployed across environments.
It enforces validation, controlled deployments, and approval gates.

## Pipeline Stages
- Checkout: Retrieves source code
- Validate: Runs basic checks before build
- Build: Builds the application artifact
- Docker Build: Packages the application into a container image
- Deploy to Dev: Automatic deployment from develop branch
- Deploy to Staging: Manual approval required from main branch

## Controls
- Branch-based deployment strategy
- Manual approval for staging releases
- Centralised pipeline logic maintained by DevOps
